    "result_text": "The build is green. Let me verify my summary of the changes is complete and coherent.\n\nAll tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures). Here's what I implemented for the `customerCode` feature:\n\n**The rule** \u2014 on registration, each owner gets a `customerCode` formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`: the upper-cased first three letters of the last name, then a global 4-digit zero-padded sequence equal to one more than the current owner count.\n\n**Changes, each in its natural home:**\n\n1. **`CustomerCodeGenerator`** (new, `service/`) \u2014 a small `@Component` with a single responsibility: pure formatting of `(lastName, sequence)` \u2192 `\"SMI-0007\"`. No persistence concerns.\n\n2. **`OwnerRepository`** \u2014 added `long count()` (Spring Data JPA derives it automatically for the `spring-data-jpa` profile; explicit implementations added to the `jpa` and `jdbc` impls so all three profiles compile and work).\n\n3. **`ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`** \u2014 orchestrates: when the owner is new and has no code yet, it fetches the count, asks the generator for the code, and sets it before saving. Updates leave an existing code untouched.\n\n4. **`Owner` entity** \u2014 added the persisted `customer_code` column with getter/setter, following the existing `email`/`registrationDate` pattern.\n\n5. **DB schemas** (hsqldb, h2, postgres, mysql) \u2014 added the `customer_code` column. The test profile uses `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema change is what makes it persist.\n\n6. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `customerCode` as a read-only property on the `Owner` response schema (alongside `displayName`/`initials`). The generated `OwnerDto` field name matches the entity getter, so MapStruct maps it with no extra mapper code.\n\nThe acceptance test confirms both the format (`SMI-`/`JON-` prefixes) and that the global sequence increments by exactly one across successive creates.",
